SUMMARY:FASEB SRC: Hippo Pathway in Biology and Disease 2026 (2nd)
LOCATION:The Fort Garry Hotel\, Spa & Conference Centre\, Winnipeg\, Canada
DESCRIPTION:Second edition of the FASEB conference on the Hippo pathway\, c
 overing mechanisms of Hippo regulation\, subcellular dynamics of Hippo sig
 nalling\, transcriptional regulation in cancer\, Hippo in stem cells and r
 egeneration\, Hippo in non-cancer disease\, and drugging the pathway for c
 ancer treatment. Unpublished data is shared throughout\, with a Meet the E
 xpert workshop and a career-development workshop for early-career research
 ers.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): The programme is about Hippo\
 , not mTOR\, but Kun-Liang Guan (Westlake University\, Hangzhou) is one of
  the four organizers\, and he is one of the five researchers the Atlas tra
 cks most closely (10 studies in the corpus). One named programme topic is 
 Hippo crosstalk with other pathways in development and disease\, which is 
 where the two growth-control networks meet\; Guan's own corpus work sits o
 n the mTOR side of that crosstalk\, from amino-acid signalling to the Rag 
 GTPases.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a profile in the Atlas: Kun-Liang 
 Guan\n\nConference site: https://events.faseb.org/Hippo-Pathways\n\nIn Oli
 ver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-faseb-src-hippo-pathwa
 y-in-biology-and-disease-2026-2nd
